{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "BgXym8IF_IN6omrXr",
	"notes": "Veteran Astra Militarum NCO who leads a ten-man infantry squad: a Guardsman who survived enough campaigns to be handed the stripes. Built from the Guardsman template with the same lore basis (Codex: Astra Militarum background on squad sergeants, and Gaunt's Ghosts and Cain-novel NCOs). Point math (see each entry's `design` field): ST 11 (+10), DX 12 (+40), IQ 10 (+0), HT 13 (+30) = 80; advantages +30 (Fit 5, Combat Reflexes 15, Military Rank 2 levels 10); disadvantages -33 (same as the Guardsman); skills +71. Total 148 points: a veteran NCO inside framework.md's \"Trained soldier (100-175)\" tier, above the 100-point line trooper. Over the Guardsman: HT +1, Military Rank 2 (sergeant), Leadership 12 pts (IQ+3 = 13), Tactics 12 pts (IQ+2 = 12), chainsword Broadsword 4 pts (DX+1 = 13), laspistol Beam Weapons (Pistol) 4 pts (DX+2 = 14), Intimidation 4 pts (Will+1 = 11). The chainsword uses Broadsword, per the weapon-skill table. Wargear (lasgun or laspistol, chainsword, flak armour) is in the wargear files, not here. The Guardsman's options carry over unchanged: Fanaticism (The God-Emperor), the world-of-origin lenses and the regimental lenses are all disabled by default; enable one regimental lens and optionally one world lens, and buy the matching skill (a lens perk raises a skill only if the character owns it; see the Guardsman notes for the list). Shared traits are pulled in with `include` from Imperium/Traits/Imperial Traits.adq per docs/data-format.md.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "t1e46t6knkU4RSlID",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Guardsman is an ordinary, healthy adult human — no augmetic or gene-therapy enhancement.\n\nDesign: ST 11 (+1 from the human baseline of 10), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 10,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "st",
					"amount": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tndEcTwhiqDIOGkb9",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Basic training drills reflexes and weapon-handling hard; Imperial Guard doctrine (per Only War's calibration and countless Gaunt's Ghosts firefights) assumes competent, not exceptional, marksmanship from line infantry.\n\nDesign: DX 12 (+2 from baseline), 20 pts/level (B15). Same as the Guardsman.",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 40,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "dx",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tEapL_c68Qq3TVgJF",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Average intelligence; the Munitorum trains doctrine and obedience, not independent thought.\n\nDesign: IQ 10 (baseline), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "tHSlXn3vy9WuBREjz",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Years of campaigning kill off the weak; a veteran sergeant is hardier than the average trooper.\n\nDesign: HT 13 (+3 from baseline), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 30,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "ht",
					"amount": 3
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tQlq3he2ZrQx9vXjG",
			"name": "Fit",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Route marches and drill leave most Guardsmen in decent physical condition.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fit (B55), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "tmUQZAPFVlpUh934J",
			"name": "Combat Reflexes",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Drilled reactions under fire: Guard doctrine relies on soldiers who don't freeze at their first firefight, since most won't survive a second chance to learn.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "thptPkkarIWPCP35C",
			"name": "Military Rank (Sergeant)",
			"reference": "B29",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A squad sergeant holds the lowest NCO rank above the troopers, commanding a ten-man squad - Codex Astra Militarum background.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Rank (B29), 5/level, 2 levels (10 points).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "tXXHPalpJ4UCB-pBF",
			"name": "Fanaticism (The God-Emperor)",
			"reference": "B136",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Optional, not baseline. Zealot regiments (Krieg's atonement culture, the Mordian Iron Guard) and individual fanatics have it; the typical Guardsman is pious but pragmatic. Enabling it adds -15 points.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fanaticism (B136), flat -15, taken for \"the Emperor/the Imperial Creed\" as the group/ideal. Not leveled in Basic Set. The Guardsman template carries it disabled: enable it for zealot regiments or characters, and conscript, penal and feral troops leave it off.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -15,
			"disabled": true
		},
		{
			"id": "tyfglWYd8_sdqkVJV",
			"name": "Duty (Astra Militarum)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Guardsmen do not resign; the Munitorum owns their service until death, discharge, or reassignment. Extremely hazardous, almost always active — front-line Guard regiments are shown fighting until they are no longer regiments.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Duty (B133): almost-always-on-duty, hazardous, involuntary military service, at the top of the disadvantage's standard cost range.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "t7n0NNZgrDgXNzi64",
			"name": "Sense of Duty (Squadmates)",
			"reference": "B153",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Small combat units live and die by cohesion; abandoning a wounded comrade is the one thing that reliably gets a soldier shunned by their own side, per how Guard squads and Sororitas/Militarum Tempestus kill-teams are consistently written in Black Library fiction.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Sense of Duty (B153), small-group scope, -5.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		},
		{
			"id": "ttUOV3fAEMQkGj6uz",
			"name": "Intolerance (Xenos)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: \"The alien is the enemy\" as baseline Imperial doctrine — not personal bigotry but state religion. Universal across Black Library fiction; only a minority of xenos-sympathetic characters (some Rogue Traders, Ordo Xenos radicals) lack it.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140). Costed at -10, the \"very broad category\" end of the range the book allows, since \"all non-human sapient species\" is about as broad a target as Intolerance can name.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "t4RcONCBj2vSr3-P3",
			"name": "Fatalistic About the Front",
			"local_notes": "Lore: \"You're already dead, trooper, you just haven't stopped moving yet\" — Guard humour about their own life expectancy.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		},
		{
			"id": "t89aHD5wEP9ZclmI7",
			"name": "Prayers, Charms and Aquila Tokens",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A trooper's private superstitions, luck-rituals and whispered prayers before a drop; observant piety, not zealotry.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only. Stands in for the baseline piety that Fanaticism no longer carries.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		},
		{
			"id": "tRErybcsBk8lVVFP_",
			"name": "Griped About the Munitorum",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Universal soldier's grumbling about rations, kit, and paperwork — never about the Emperor.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		},
		{
			"id": "TWxKk94TF1uk4TtnV",
			"name": "Hive World Origin",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Born and raised inside a hive's vertical city-machine: gang territories, recycled air, and a horizon that is always a wall. Calibrated against Only War's Hive World home-world package (bonus to Fellowship/streetwise-type skills, poor grasp of open terrain) and against Necromunda's depiction throughout Black Library.\n\nDesign: A small optional container (net 0 points) rather than a full racial template: two Basic Set perks/quirks bought as a set, per framework.md's instruction to keep origin lenses lore-flavoured rather than mechanically heavy. Disabled by default in templates; the GM/player enables the one that fits.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "t74l7BSB-K7gMEprU",
					"name": "Hive-Bred",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A lifetime spent reading crowds, gangs, and hab-block politics.\n\nDesign: Perk (B9), +1 to Streetwise.",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": 1,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
							"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Streetwise"
							},
							"amount": 1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tyVl1C9hcNh8ZmzM9",
					"name": "Never Seen an Open Sky",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Hivers are famously unsettled by true horizons and weather.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only, no mechanical effect.",
					"tags": [
						"Quirk",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -1
				}
			],
			"disabled": true
		},
		{
			"id": "T7n-9CRP2zWystTaP",
			"name": "Death World Origin",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Raised on a world that actively tries to kill its population — the Catachan/Krieg-adjacent archetype. Only War's Death World package (bonus to combat/survival skills, penalty to Fellowship from a lifetime of mistrust) is the calibration source.\n\nDesign: Net 0 points, two Basic Set perks/quirks. Disabled by default; GM/player enables it.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "t9cElEOww2WQM9mnQ",
					"name": "Death World Instincts",
					"local_notes": "Lore: A childhood spent not being eaten teaches attentiveness other worlds don't.\n\nDesign: Perk (B9), +1 to Survival.",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": 1,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
							"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Survival"
							},
							"amount": 1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tBHlPEAQUWWcux4Uz",
					"name": "Contempt for Soft Living",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Hive worlds and their comforts look like weakness from a death world's perspective.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
					"tags": [
						"Quirk",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -1
				}
			],
			"disabled": true
		},
		{
			"id": "T-BPr3w9kW_h2s20I",
			"name": "Feral World Origin",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A pre-industrial or tribal Imperial world (the kind that furnishes the Imperium with superstitious but ferocious Guard regiments and occasional Space Marine recruits, as with Fenris or Chogoris in Astartes lore). Only War's Feral World package (combat/melee bonus, Tech-Use penalty) is the calibration source.\n\nDesign: Net 0 points, two Basic Set perks/quirks. Disabled by default; GM/player enables it.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tO1VEfTCp6k1LEBRq",
					"name": "Warrior's Upbringing",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Trained from childhood to fight with whatever the tribe carries.\n\nDesign: Perk (B9), +1 to Spear (or the tribe's usual melee weapon skill; swap the key to match).",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": 1,
					"features": [
